  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing demand-driven expertise and capacity strengthening through the GTH 2.0 in the areas of settlement profiling and planning, optimized water systems, flood risk management, renewable energy, climate security, and sustainable procurement supporting more resilient and locally led responses</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Given the resource constraints and operational pressures faced in many crisis contexts, there is a pressing need to pool technical expertise and financial resources across agencies and actors, beyond traditional knowledge already available. Shared approaches and collaborative investments not only reduce duplication but also ensure that innovative solutions and lessons learned are made widely available. This approach is more efficient, as it allows limited resources&#x2014;technical, financial, and human&#x2014;to be shared and used strategically across a wide range of actors and contexts. In highly dynamic and resource-limited environments, the ability to share outcomes&#x2014;both successes and setbacks&#x2014;is essential for scaling up new effective practices, avoiding mistakes, and building collective technical capacity.GTH 2.0 responds directly to this need and aims at improving the quality and impact of humanitarian programming by focusing on: Sustainable and resilient solutions, Integrated Approaches, and Promoting Local Engagement and Contextual Solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
